TI  - A Prospective Randomized Controlled Study to Compare Efficacy of Caspofungin Combined With Trimethoprim-sulfamethoxazole Versus Trimethoprim/Sulfamethoxazole as First-line Therapy in Non-HIV Patients With Severe Pneumocystis Pneumonia
AU  - Anonymous.
T2  - clinicaltrials.gov
AB  - Brief Summary, This is a prospective, randomized clinical trial. During the study, non-HIV patients who are admitted to ICU due to Pneumocystic pneumonia (PCP) and have not received anti-PCP therapy or have received therapy less than 48hrs will be randomized (1:1) to received caspofungin combined with trimethoprim-sulfamethoxazole or trimethoprim-sulfamethoxazole alone. The aim of this study is to compare the effectiveness of caspofungin combined with trimethoprim-sulfamethoxazole with that of conventional therapy (trimethoprim-sulfamethoxazole alone) as first-line therapy in the treatment of severe Pneumocystis pneumonia (PCP) in non-HIV patients.Copyright © 2025 clinicaltrials.gov
